{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create an unprivileged helpdesk account on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account was absent initially, then existed as UID/GID 1000 with its own group only, a home directory, and a set password. It remained intact after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-152e008bddd2473a","cmd-f288f7a45b424c4c","cmd-0cf288926d1045f0"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow helpdesk to restart the SSH service with sudo.","status":"satisfied","summary":"From a healthy SSH baseline, helpdesk successfully invoked the permitted sudo restart. The changed PID and invocation identity demonstrate a real restart, followed by an active service, listeners, and successful SSH handshake. The behavior was repeated successfully after node reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c5bca6f339734d98","cmd-2b67cc3a71dd4652","cmd-9f437bcc48094720"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Grant helpdesk no other administrative privileges.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Helpdesk belongs only to its own group, and its effective sudo listing contains only the two equivalent SSH restart forms. Authenticated attempts to run root id, stop SSH, restart crond, and obtain a root shell were denied before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c5bca6f339734d98","cmd-2f5fd5ade6e94264","cmd-f2c47b4998324747"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account provisioning, the sudoers policy, bounded SSH restart tests, and the mandatory reboot all had direct task or evidence roles. Temporary sudoers staging was trap-cleaned. The retained password recovery copy was used for authenticated denial tests and remained root-owned mode 0600. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, no package damage, no additional exposed sockets, and only normal reboot-related replacement of systemd private temporary directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f288f7a45b424c4c","cmd-ff6f56b206684e59","cmd-2b67cc3a71dd4652","cmd-7628db454ab64e11","cmd-0cf288926d1045f0","cmd-9f437bcc48094720","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the post-restart identity changed and agrees with the fixed lifecycle observations, and system health, SSH behavior, account state, and sudo policy recovered successfully.","limitations":["Fixed lifecycle probes do not inventory local accounts or sudoers, so those objects are independently observed only through executor commands after reboot.","The privilege-negative evidence covers group membership, the effective sudo policy, and representative authenticated denial tests, but does not audit every conceivable non-sudo privilege mechanism."]}
